# NOT /Dockerfile and NOT /.dockerignore. Both are shipped artefacts of this
# repo -- they build the published ghcr.io/tina4stack/tina4-php base image.
# Dockerfile was already tracked (a rule cannot un-track a tracked file), but
# .dockerignore was genuinely ignored, so its `**/vendor` exclusion existed only
# on one laptop. Without that exclusion the image does not boot at all, so the
# fix has to be in the repo. The other three framework repos track theirs.
/src/public/css/base.css
/src/public/css/colors.css
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
example/.env
example/vendor/
example/data/*.db
example/data/*.db-*
example/data/sessions/
example/logs/
tests/logs/*.log
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
/data/sessions/
/data/
/nonexistent_path/
.tina4/

# Test/scratch artifacts. tmp/tina4-mx-php.db was COMMITTED, which made
# SqliteAbsolutePathParityTest unpassable on Linux: the test asserts no
# cwd-relative shadow directory was created, and on Linux sys_get_temp_dir()
# is /tmp, so the first path segment it checks is exactly this directory.
tmp/

# A stray SQLite database literally named "sqlite::memory:" was committed at the
# repo root: the in-memory DSN reached the SQLite adapter with its scheme still
# attached, so resolveDatabasePath() treated it as a cwd-relative file and
# SQLite created it. Its colon makes the repo impossible to clone on Windows.
# Ignore it so it can never return; Database::create() already normalises the
# documented "sqlite::memory:" URL to ":memory:" before the adapter sees it.
/sqlite::memory:
